<title>MEXICO: Banamex loans $15 mln to CIPSA.</title>
<headline>Banamex loans $15 mln to CIPSA.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Nacional de Mexico SA (Banamex) said on Thursday it had agreed to a $15 million loan for Compania Industrial de Parras SA de CV (CIPSA).</p>
<p>CIPSA, Mexico's top maker of denim, will used the loan to boost its export program and to consolidate some of its 10-year debts, Banamex said in a news release.</p>
<p>Banamex, the banking unit of Grupo Financiero Banamex-Accival, is Mexico's largest bank.</p>
<p>Terms of the loan were not announced.</p>
<p>((--Dan Trotta, Mexico City newsroom, +525 728-9507))</p>
